{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"community-sediment-snipe","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nDiscovered during the Step 7 parity census for bug `5931-78a3-95d2-44cd`. On Jira Data\nCenter the outbound comment send path applies **no length fit at all**, so an\nover-length comment is handed to Jira unfitted.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/_links.py:82-84` — `_CommentsMixin.add_comment` passes `body`\n  straight to `self._client.add_comment(remote_id, body)`; no fit, no sanitize.\n- `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:493-494` — `JiraDCBackend.add_comment` is a bare\n  delegate to that transport.\n- `_DCSanitizer.sanitize_comment` (`backend.py:259-273`) — the send-side sanitizer with\n  its operator warning — has **no production caller**. `grep -rn \"\\.sanitize_comment(\" src tests`\n  returns test files ONLY (`test_dc_comment_ceiling_049e.py`,\n  `test_dc_backend_characterization.py`, `test_backend_characterization.py`). The same is\n  true for Cloud's `_JiraSanitizer.sanitize_comment`.\n- `fit_comment` (the differ-side twin) IS wired, via `outbound_comments._diff_comments`.\n  So the comparison half of the convergence pair is live and the SEND half is not.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nBug `6afc-20ee-84e5-4dd5` established that Jira exits 0 on an over-length comment\nrejection, so the comment never lands and is re-emitted every pass — the outbound\ncomment-sync loop. DC's ceiling is lower than Cloud's and is deployment-resolved\n(`comment_max_chars()`, bug `049e`), which makes an unfitted DC body more likely to be\nrejected, not less. `test_dc_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py` pins the CONTRACT\nbut not the WIRING.\n\nNote this is NOT bug 5931's mechanism — with no truncation on the DC path there is\nnothing to cut the RECONCILER_MARKER off. It is the mirror-image gap found by the same\ncensus: Cloud truncates and loses the marker; DC does not truncate at all.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The DC outbound comment send path fits the body through the deployment-resolved\n      ceiling before handing it to the transport.\n- [ ] A test drives the DC send path with an over-length body and asserts the wire value\n      is within `comment_max_chars()` (RED on current code).\n- [ ] Cloud's `sanitize_comment` is either wired or removed — a send-side sanitizer with\n      no caller is a false assurance.","id":"b9b4-f460-2d54-4872","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Jira DC outbound comments are never length-fitted: sanitize_comment has no production caller"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787293635834766001,"uuid":"629297d0-9cbe-4571-a0a5-7adf96835735"}